<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-30">30 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Cortés flees Tenochtitlan on the Noche Triste</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Under attack by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a>, Cortés's forces fought their way out of the city along the causeways at night, losing hundreds of Spaniards and many more Tlaxcalan allies. He returned to besiege it in 1521.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-28">28 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Magellan's ships enter the Pacific</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After 38 days navigating the strait at the tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan">Ferdinand Magellan</a>'s three remaining ships reached the open ocean. He named it the Pacific for its calm waters.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-10">10 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Luther burns the papal bull against him</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a>'s Elster Gate, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> burned Leo X's bull threatening him with excommunication, along with books of canon law. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> excommunicated him the following month.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-raichur" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-raichur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-raichur">Battle of Raichur</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Raichur was fought in 1520 between the Vijayanagara Empire under Krishnadevaraya and the Bijapur Sultanate under Ismail Adil Shah near the fortress of Raichur in the Deccan.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm-bloodbath" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stockholm-bloodbath.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/stockholm-bloodbath">Stockholm Bloodbath</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Stockholm Bloodbath was the mass execution of some eighty Swedish nobles, clergy and burghers in Stockholm in November 1520, ordered by Christian II of Denmark after his conquest of Sweden.</p></div></li></ol></section>
